ms/modifiers | **Kept** – it is the exported contract and likely to grow beyond quoting |\n| `basePremiumForItem(item)` | Lookup base premium for a single item | **Renamed** to `basePremiumForType(type)` – it only needs the type string, so the old name and `Item` parameter were misleading |\n| `componentBlockPremium(type, count)` | Calculated premium for *any* group of component-type items, block or not | **Renamed** to `basePremiumForItemGroup(type, count)` – old name implied it only handled block pricing |\n| `sumBasePremiums(items)` | Sums base premiums across grouped items | **Kept** – clearly describes its role |\n| `counts` | Local tally of items per type | **Renamed** to `itemTypeCounts` – removes ambiguity in `sumBasePremiums` |\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\nScope: premium-calculation logic (`basePremiumForType`, `basePremiumForItemGroup`, `sumBasePremiums`, `processScenario`). The static `BASE_PREMIUMS` lookup table is excluded because it is unchanged data.\n\nCounting assumptions:\n- **Bindings**: parameters and local variables\n- **Constants**: primitive literals in logic\n- **Invocations**: function/method/constructor calls, bracket access, binary operators (`+`, `*`, `===`, `&&`, `??`, etc.)\n- **Conditionals**: `if`, `switch`, ternary\n- **Loops**: `for...of`\n- **Assignments**: mutations / compound assignments\n\n### Initial Mass\n\n| Function | Bindings | Constants | Invocations | Conditionals | Loops | Assignments | Subtotal |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| `basePremiumForItem` | 1 | 0 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 3 |\n| `componentBlockPremium` | 2 | 0 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 9 |\n| `sumBasePremiums` | 6 | 3 | 11 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 46 |\n| `processScenario` | 2 | 0 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 7 |\n| **Totals** | **11** | **3** | **21** | **2** | **2** | **2** | **65** |\n\n`65 = 11 + 3 + 21 + (2×4) + (2×5) + (2×6)`\n\n### Final Mass\n\n| Function | Bindings | Constants | Invocations | Conditionals | Loops | Assignments | Subtotal |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---: