IZE) {\n    return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumForType(type);\n};\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const itemTypeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    itemTypeCounts[item.type] = (itemTypeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(itemTypeCounts)) {\n    total += basePremiumForItemGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (\n  scenario: Scenario\n): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const itemsToQuote = scenario.steps[0]?.items ?? [];\n  return {\n    results: [{ premium: sumBasePremiums(itemsToQuote) + PROCESSING_FEE }],\n  };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923510737},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now produce final report. We need to include:\n- Naming evaluation decisions.\n- Initial and final APP mass calculations with component counts.\n- Simple design rule evaluation.\n- Tests status.\n- Summary.\n\nNeed to be careful with the mass numbers. Let's recalculate with final file to ensure consistency.\n\nWe'll define the scope: premium-calculation logic functions and `processScenario`. Excluding the static `BASE_PREMIUMS` lookup table (constants unchanged). But we can also present absolute with note. Let's present the logic mass and note data table excluded. The component count table should be clear.\n\nInitial code (before refactoring) logic mass:\nFunctions: basePremiumForItem, componentBlockPremium, sumBasePremiums, processScenario.\n\nLet's make a table per function.\n\nAssumptions:\n- Bindings: parameters and local variables.\n- Constants: primitive numeric/string literals in logic.\n- Invocations: function/method calls, constructor calls, array/object bracket access, binary operators (including `??`, `===`, `&&`, `+`, `*`), optional chaining (`?.`).\n- Conditionals: `if`/`switch`/ternary.\n- Loops: `for...of`.\n- Assignments: `=