+ 10) where 10 is 10% of 150? 10% of (100+50) = 15. But they say 10. Let me re-read: \"(100 G base + 50 G curse + 10 G first insurance = 160 G + 5 G fee = 165 G)\". So first insurance is 10 G, which is 10% of the base 100, not of (base+curse). Hmm, so the first insurance surcharge applies to the policy base premium (sum of item base premiums), not after item modifiers.\n\nFrom spec: \"item-specific modifiers (cursed, high enchantment) apply to the base premium of the affected item; policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract) apply to the policy base premium (the sum of all item base premiums)\".\n\nSo:\n- item modified base = item base * itemFactor\n- policy base = sum of item base premiums (unmodified)\n- policy modified base = policy base * policyFactor\n- total premium = sum(item modified base) + (policy modified base - policy base) + fee? \n\nWait, let's check integration:\n- Newcomer cursed sword: item base = 100, item modified = 150. Policy base = 100. First insurance 10% of policy base = 10. Total = 150 + 10 + 5 = 165. ✓\n- Long-standing second contract cursed sword enchant 7: item base = 100, item modified = 100 + 50 + 30 = 180. Policy base = 100. Policy modifiers: loyalty -20% of 100 = -20, first insurance +10% = +10, follow-up -15% = -15. Net policy modifier = -25. Total = 180 - 25 + 5 = 160. ✓\n- Multi-item cursed sword + amulet: item bases = 100, 60. Policy base = 160. Item modified = 150 + 60 = 210. First insurance = 16. Total = 210 + 16 = 226? But spec says 210 before further modifiers and fee, then + fee = 215? Wait: \"policy base premium 160 G; the cursed surcharge adds 50 G (50 % of the cursed sword's base premium, not of the policy total) → 210 G before further modifiers and fee\". So after item modifiers it's 210. Then policy-wide first insurance (10% of policy base 160) = 16. Total = 210 + 16 + 5 = 231? But the example says \"→ 210 G before further modifiers and fee\" implying policy modifiers apply after. But they didn't