ex. But it's necessary for correctness.\n\nFor now, let me focus on getting test 14 passing and update the other quote tests. Let me update the implementation with first insurance and rounding.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Maybe the \"first insurance\" surcharge applies only to the policy base, and if the customer has previous quotes in the scenario, it's different. But for single-step tests, it's the first quote, so +10%.\n\nAlso, the \"follow-up contract\" discount: 15% off each contract after the first. So for first quote, no discount. For second quote in scenario, -15% on policy base.\n\nLet me update the implementation to:\n- compute policyBase = sumBasePremiums with blocks and item modifiers? Wait no, policy-wide modifiers apply to policy base which is sum of item base premiums (unmodified).\n\nRe-reading: \"policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract) apply to the policy base premium (the sum of all item base premiums)\".\n\nSo policy base = sum of unmodified item base premiums (with block discount).\n\nThen:\n- itemModifiedTotal = sum over items of (itemBase * itemFactor)\n- policyBase = sum of itemBase (with blocks)\n- policyModifierAmount = policyBase * (firstInsurance + loyalty + followUp factors)\n- total = itemModifiedTotal + policyModifierAmount + fee\n- round up\n\nFor cursed sword:\n- itemModifiedTotal = 100 * 1.5 = 150\n- policyBase = 100\n- policyModifierAmount = 100 * 0.1 = 10\n- total = 150 + 10 + 5 = 165 ✓\n\nFor plain sword:\n- itemModifiedTotal = 100\n- policyBase = 100\n- policyModifierAmount = 100 * 0.1 = 10\n- total = 100 + 10 + 5 = 115\n\nThis makes sense.\n\nBut for components, item modifiers don't apply. And first insurance applies to policy base.\n\nNow I need to update tests 2-13. Let me do a bulk edit of the test file. This is a lot, but necessary.\n\nActually wait - maybe I should not update old tests and instead make first insurance not apply by default? No, that would be wrong per spec.\n\nAlternative: maybe the \"first insurance\" surcharge doesn't apply when the scenario has only one quote step? No, the spec says \"A first insurance carries a 10 % initial assessment surcharge.\" It's about the contract, not the scenario. Each quote is a first insurance for that item set. The integration example says \"each item in a quote is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history.\" So yes, every quote has first insurance unless it's a follow-up contract (second quote in scenario).\n\nSo every single-step quote test should include first insurance.\n\nLet me update all quote tests. I'll read the current test file and update the expectations.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:95","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":538,"output":2761,"cacheRead":56704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2740,"totalTokens":60003,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784923564437,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4afbea55-2975-4b78-a7a2-ff1ccbd320d9","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:95","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quotes\n  it(\"should quote an empty item list at 5 G -- only the processing fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword at 105 G -- 100 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 105 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet at 65 G -- 60 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 65 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff at 85 G -- 80 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 85 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion at 45 G -- 40 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 45 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune at 30 G -- 25 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 30 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone at 30 G -- 25 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 30 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Component blocks\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes at 55 G -- 50 G base + 5 G fee (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 55 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 3 runes at 65 G -- 60 G block base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 65 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes at 105 G -- 100 G base + 5 G fee (block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 105 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes at 180 G -- 175 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n        ],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 180 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes + 1 moonstone at 80 G -- 75 G base + 5 G fee (different types)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 80 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 3 runes + 3 moonstones at 125 G -- 120 G base + 5 G fee (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        ],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 125 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Item modifiers\n  it(\"should apply a 50% cursed surcharge to a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 30% high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment >= 5 -- premium 145 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4 -- premium 115 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges when both apply\");\n\n  // Customer and contract modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 20% loyalty discount for customers with >= 2 years\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 10% first-insurance surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 15% follow-up contract discount after the first contract\");\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should quote a newcomer with a cursed sword at 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed highly-enchanted sword at 160 G\");\n\n  // Multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific cursed surcharge only to the cursed item -- cursed sword + plain amulet = 215 G\");\n\n  // Claims\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for regular sword damage 500 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 100 G for rune damage 200 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse a dragon-material sword -- 700 G for damage 800 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse 50% for an item with enchantment >= 8 -- 400 G for damage 1000 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply the 50% enchantment rule when both dragon material and enchantment >= 8 apply -- 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply the 100 G deductible per damaged item -- 600 G for sword 500 G + amulet 300 G\");\n\n  // Caps and mult