remium` → `calculateQuotePremium`; dropped the now-unused `customer` and `quoteIndex` parameters.\n3. Renamed `itemModifierFactor` → `itemPremiumMultiplier`.\n4. Extracted `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE` and `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE` constants.\n5. Rewrote `itemPremiumMultiplier` as a pure expression, removing mutable `let`/`+=`.\n\n**APP Mass (executable code only)**\n\n| Component | Before | After |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Constants | 21 | 24 |\n| Bindings | 21 | 19 |\n| Invocations | 12 → 24 | 11 → 22 |\n| Conditionals | 7 → 28 | 7 → 28 |\n| Loops | 3 → 15 | 3 → 15 |\n| Assignments | 18 → 108 | 18 → 108 |\n| **Total** | **217** | **216** |\n\nMass is essentially unchanged; the real improvement is intent (Rule 2), which takes priority over mass.\n\n**Simple Design Rules**\n1. Tests Pass: all 14 passing tests remain green.\n2. Reveals Intent: surcharge rates and the first-insurance surcharge are now explicit and self-documenting.\n3. No Duplication: no duplicated code found; no new duplication introduced.\n4. Fewest Elements: removed the unused-parameter function and the mutable multiplier variable.\n\n**Result**\nTests: 14 passed, 24 todo. Code is in `src/claim-office.ts`."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Added item-level modifiers (cursed +50%, enchantment >=5 +30%), first-insurance policy-wide +10%, and group-base sharing so component block discounts are preserved.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Added item-level modifiers (cursed +50%, enchantment >=5 +30%), first-insurance policy-wide +10%, and group-base sharing so component block discounts are preserved.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784923615770},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the test file and implementation file to understand what needs to be refactored.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":110,"output":60,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":22,"totalTokens":5738,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784923615790,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d07df1cc-47e8-4d4c-a2c0-c1d7b963429f","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quotes\n  it(\"should quote an empty item list at 5 G -- only the processing fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword at 115 G -- 100 G base + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet at 71 G -- 60 G base + 6 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff at 93 G -- 80 G base + 8 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion at 49 G -- 40 G base + 4 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune at 33 G -- 25 G base + 3 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone at 33 G -- 25 G base + 3 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Component blocks\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes at 60 G -- 50 G base + 5 G first insurance + 5 G fee (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 3 runes at 71 G -- 60 G block base + 6 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes at 115 G -- 100 G base + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee (block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes at 198 G -- 175 G base + 18 G first insurance + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n        ],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes + 1 moonstone at 88 G -- 75 G base + 8 G first insurance + 5 G fee (different types)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 3 runes + 3 moonstones at 137 G -- 120 G base + 12 G first insurance + 5 G fee (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        ],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Item modifiers\n  it(\"should apply a 50% cursed surcharge to a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{\n        op: \"quote\",\n        items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }],\n      }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 30% high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment >= 5 -- premium 145 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4 -- premium 115 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges when both apply\");\n\n  // Customer and contract modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 20% loyalty discount for customers with >= 2 years\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 10% first-insurance surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply a 15% follow-up contract discount after the first contract\");\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should quote a newcomer with a cursed sword at 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed highly-enchanted sword at 160 G\");\n\n  // Multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific cursed surcharge only to the cursed item -- cursed sword + plain amulet = 215 G\");\n\n  // Claims\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for regular sword damage 500 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 100 G for rune damage 200 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse a dragon-material sword -- 700 G for damage 800 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse 50% for an item with enchantment >= 8 -- 400 G for damage 1000 G after 100 G deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply the 50% enchantment rule when both dragon material and enchantment >= 8 apply -- 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply the 100 G deductible per damaged item -- 600 G for sword 500 G + amulet 300 G\");\n\n  // Caps and multiple items\n  it.todo(\"should compute insurance sum 2000 G and cap 4000 G for two swords\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat each damage entry as a separate damage with its own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce payout to remaining cap when cap is exhausted -- first 1400 G, then 600 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim with more damage entries than insured items\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit non-zero for an unknown item type in a quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit non-zero for an unknown item type in a claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit non-zero for a negative damage amount\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round a premium up in MHPCO favor -- 197.5 G becomes 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round a payout down in MHPCO favor -- 350.5 G becomes 350 G\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923617334},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\n\ninterface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n}\n\ninterface ScenarioStep {\n  op: string;\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: ScenarioStep[];\n}\n\nconst basePremiumForType = (type: string): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst basePremiumForItemGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES.has(type) && count === BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumForType(type);\n};\n\nconst itemModifierFactor = (item: Item): number => {\n  let factor = 1;\n  if (item.cursed) {\n    factor += 0.5;\n  }\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n    factor += 0.3;\n  }\n  return factor;\n};\n\nconst policyWideFactor = (_customer: Customer, _quoteIndex: number): number => {\n  // First insurance surcharge applies to every quote; follow-up discount handled later.\n  return 1.1;\n};\n\nconst roundUp = (value: number): number => Math.ceil(value - 0.0001);\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[], customer: Customer, quoteIndex: number): number => {\n  const itemTypeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    itemTypeCounts[item.type] = (itemTypeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  const policyBase = Object.entries(itemTypeCounts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + basePremiumForItemGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n  const itemModifiedTotal = items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    const groupBase = basePremiumForItemGroup(item.type, itemTypeCounts[item.type]);\n    const share = groupBase / itemTypeCounts[item.type];\n    return sum + share * itemModifierFactor(item);\n  }, 0);\n  const total = itemModifiedTotal + policyBase * (policyWideFactor(customer, quoteIndex) - 1) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUp(total);\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (\n  scenario: Scenario\n): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const itemsToQuote = scenario.steps[0]?.items ?? [];\n  return {\n    results: [{ premium: quotePremium(itemsToQuote, scenario.customer, 0) }],\n  };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923617334},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the current code and tests. Currently 14 tests pass, including the new tests for cursed items, first-insurance policy-wide +10%, and group-base sharing for component block discounts.\n\nLet me understand the implementation:\n\n1. `PROCESSING_FEE = 5` - constant processing fee\n2. `BASE_PREMIUMS` - base premiums by type\n3. `DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM = 100` - default if type not found\n4. `basePremiumForType` - gets base premium for type\n5. `COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES` - rune, moonstone\n6. `BLOCK_SIZE = 3`\n7. `BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60`\n8. `basePremiumForItemGroup` - if component block type and count == 3, return 60, else count * base\n9. `itemModifierFactor` - cursed +50%, enchantment >=5 +30%\n10. `policyWideFactor` - returns 1.1 (first insurance surcharge)\n11. `roundUp` - Math.ceil(value - 0.0001)\n12. `quotePremium` - calculates premium\n13. `processScenario` - main function\n\nLet me think about issues with the current code:\n\n1. Naming issues:\n   - `policyWideFactor` - returns a factor, but the name doesn't clearly capture that it only applies the first-insurance surcharge. It ignores customer and quoteIndex parameters, which is suspicious. The comment says \"First insurance surcharge applies to every quote; follow-up discount handled later.\" But \"later\" doesn't exist. Actually, the function returns 1.1 always.\n   - `basePremiumForItemGroup` - name is okay, but maybe `componentBlock` should be clearer.\n   - `quotePremium` - does more than quote a premium, it calculates a premium.\n   - `processScenario` - takes a scenario but only processes the first step.\n\n2. Duplication / clarity:\n   - The group-base sharing logic in `itemModifiedTotal` is complex. It calculates `groupBase` repeatedly for each item of the same type. This is duplicated work.\n   - The calculation `policyBase * (policyWideFactor(customer, quoteIndex) - 1)` is a bit odd. Since policyWideFactor always returns 1.1, this is `policyBase * 0.1`, which is the first-insurance surcharge.\n   - `itemModifiedTotal` and `policyBase` are separate but related concepts.\n\n3. Logic issues:\n   - The component block discount is not preserved for items with modifiers. The group base is sh