r","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 33\nRecent changes: Added `validateDamages` to throw when claim damages exceed insured items per type.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":263,"output":185,"cacheRead":115136,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":115584,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924690854,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b540dc8d-9b5f-4a5c-9dae-ffc6d78c1bbf","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:196","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring Complete.\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n- `insuranceValueForType` – name still fits; it returns the insured value for an item type.\n- `enchantmentClaimMultiplier` – the name was too claim-centric. It actually returns the damage multiplier based on the item's enchantment, so it was renamed to `enchantmentDamageMultiplier`.\n\n## Initial APP Mass (insurance-value abstraction)\n\n```ts\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\nconst DEFAULT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 0;\n\nconst insuranceValueForType = (type: string): number =>\n  INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? DEFAULT_INSURANCE_VALUE;\n\nconst totalInsuranceValueFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForType(item.type), 0);\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n| Component     | Count | Mass |\n|---------------|-------|------|\n| Constants     | 7     | 7    |\n| Bindings      | 5     | 5    |\n| Invocations   | 2     | 4    |\n| Conditionals  | 1     | 4    |\n| Loops         | 1     | 5    |\n| Assignments   | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**     |       | **22** |\n\n## Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Removed duplicated insurance-value table**  \n   `INSURANCE_VALUES` repeated the same data already present in `BASE_PREMIUMS` (insurance value = base premium × 10). Replaced it with a single multiplier constant and derived the value from `BASE_PREMIUMS`. This respects **Rule 3: No Duplication** and **Rule 4: Fewest Elements**.\n\n2. **Moved `DEDUCTIBLE` and `POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER` to the top-level constants block**  \n   They are configuration constants and are now grouped with the other configuration values, removing forward-reference oddities and improving readability (**Rule 2: Reveals Intent**).\n\n3. **Renamed `enchantmentClaimMultiplier` to `enchantmentDamageMultiplier`**  \n   The new name better reflects that the function returns the multiplier applied to a damage amount (**Rule 2**).\n\n## New APP Mass (insurance-value abstraction)\n\n```ts\nconst insuranceValueForType = (type: string): number =>\n  (BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0) * INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst totalInsuranceValueFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForType(item.type), 0);\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n| Component     | Count | Mass |\n|---------------|-------|------|\n| Constants     | 2     | 2    |\n| Bindings      | 4     | 4    |\n| Invocations   | 2     | 4    |\n| Conditionals  | 1     | 4    |\n| Loops         | 1     | 5    |\n| Assignments   | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**     |       | **16** |\n\n**Mass change:** `22 → 16` (−6)\n\n## Tests\n\nAll tests remain green:\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  33 passed | 5 todo (38)\n```"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: