centric. It actually returns the damage multiplier based on the item's enchantment, so it was renamed to `enchantmentDamageMultiplier`.\n\n## Initial APP Mass (insurance-value abstraction)\n\n```ts\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\nconst DEFAULT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 0;\n\nconst insuranceValueForType = (type: string): number =>\n  INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? DEFAULT_INSURANCE_VALUE;\n\nconst totalInsuranceValueFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForType(item.type), 0);\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n| Component     | Count | Mass |\n|---------------|-------|------|\n| Constants     | 7     | 7    |\n| Bindings      | 5     | 5    |\n| Invocations   | 2     | 4    |\n| Conditionals  | 1     | 4    |\n| Loops         | 1     | 5    |\n| Assignments   | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**     |       | **22** |\n\n## Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Removed duplicated insurance-value table**  \n   `INSURANCE_VALUES` repeated the same data already present in `BASE_PREMIUMS` (insurance value = base premium × 10). Replaced it with a single multiplier constant and derived the value from `BASE_PREMIUMS`. This respects **Rule 3: No Duplication** and **Rule 4: Fewest Elements**.\n\n2. **Moved `DEDUCTIBLE` and `POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER` to the top-level constants block**  \n   They are configuration constants and are now grouped with the other configuration values, removing forward-reference oddities and improving readability (**Rule 2: Reveals Intent**).\n\n3. **Renamed `enchantmentClaimMultiplier` to `enchantmentDamageMultiplier`**  \n   The new name better reflects that the function returns the multiplier applied to a damage amount (**Rule 2**).\n\n## New APP Mass (insurance-value abstraction)\n\n```ts\nconst insuranceValueForType = (type: string): number =>\n  (BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0) * INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst totalInsuranceValueFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForType(item.type), 0);\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n| Component     | Count | Mass |\n|---------------|-------|------|\n| Constants     | 2     | 2    |\n| Bindings      | 4     | 4    |\n| Invocations   | 2     | 4    |\n| Conditionals  | 1     | 4    |\n| Loops         | 1     | 5    |\n| Assignments   | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**     |       | **16** |\n\n**Mass change:** `22 → 16` (−6)\n\n## Tests\n\nAll tests remain green:\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  33 passed | 5 todo (38)\n```"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1939,"output":2286,"cacheRead":19648,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1533,"totalTokens":23873,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784924751869,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-446fda66-71e9-4f6e-9157-5c1c718ceb21","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":8374,"output":10049,"cacheRead":65920,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":23873,"turns":5},"model":"requesty/tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784924765673},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verify file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:197","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":833,"output":24,"cacheRead":115520,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":116377,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924765683,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-51b558fa-bd25-49ec-bd04-d71de09ed3e3","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:197","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER = 10;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\n\ninterface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n}\n\ninterface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\ninterface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\ninterface ScenarioStep {\n  op: string;\n  items?: Item[];\n  policy?: number;\n  incident?: Incident;\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: ScenarioStep[];\n}\n\nconst basePremiumForType = (type: string): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst basePremiumForItemGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES.has(type) && count === BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumForType(type);\n};\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\n\nconst itemPremiumMultiplier = (item: Item): number =>\n  1 +\n  (item.cursed ? CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0) +\n  ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5 ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0);\n\n// Tiny epsilon avoids floating-point artifacts (e.g. 197.5000000001) from pushing\n// a value that should round to N up to N+1.\nconst ROUNDING_EPSILON = 0.0001;\nconst roundUp = (value: number): number => Math.ceil(value - ROUNDING_EPSILON);\n\nconst countItemsByType = (items: Item[]): Record<string, number> => {\n  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst insuranceValueForType = (type: string): number =>\n  (BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0) * INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst totalInsuranceValueFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForType(item.type), 0);\n\nconst policyCapFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  totalInsuranceValueFor(items) * POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst totalBasePremiumFor = (itemTypeCounts: Record<string, number>): number =>\n  Object.entries(itemTypeCounts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + basePremiumForItemGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\nconst totalModifiedItemPremiumFor = (\n  items: Item[],\n  itemTypeCounts: Record<string, number>\n): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    const groupBase = basePremiumForItemGroup(item.type, itemTypeCounts[item.type]);\n    const share = groupBase / itemTypeCounts[item.type];\n    return sum + share * itemPremiumMultiplier(item);\n  }, 0);\n\nconst netQuoteModifierFor = (\n  policyBase: number,\n  customer: Customer,\n  contractIndex: number\n): number => {\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount =\n    contractIndex > 0 ? policyBase * FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  return firstInsuranceSurcharge - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  contractIndex: number\n): number => {\n  const itemTypeCounts = countItemsByType(items);\n  const policyBase = totalBasePremiumFor(itemTypeCounts);\n  const totalModifiedItemPremium = totalModifiedItemPremiumFor(items, itemTypeCounts);\n  const modifier = netQuoteModifierFor(policyBase, customer, contractIndex);\n  return roundUp(totalModifiedItemPremium + modifier + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; cap: number };\ntype StepResult = { premium?: number; payout?: number; remainingCap?: number };\n\nconst enchantmentDamageMultiplier = (damage: Damage, policyItems: Item[]): number => {\n  const item = policyItems.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n  return (item?.enchantment ?? 0) >= 8 ? 0.5 : 1;\n};\n\nconst validateDamages = (damages: Damage[], policyItems: Item[]): void => {\n  const itemTypeCounts = countItemsByType(policyItems);\n  const damageTypeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (!itemTypeCounts[damage.itemType]) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} is not insured`);\n    }\n    damageTypeCounts[damage.itemType] = (damageTypeCounts[damage.itemType] ?? 0) + 1;\n    if (damageTypeCounts[damage.itemType] > itemTypeCounts[damage.itemType]) {\n      throw new Error(`More damages than insured items for type ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst calculateClaimResult = (\n  policyCap: number,\n  step: ScenarioStep,\n  policyItems: Item[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const damages = step.incident?.damages ?? [];\n  validateDamages(damages, policyItems);\n  return damages.reduce(\n    ({ payout, remainingCap }, damage) => {\n      const multiplier = enchantmentDamageMultiplier(damage, policyItems);\n      const afterDeductible = Math.max(0, damage.amount * multiplier - DEDUCTIBLE);\n      const nextPayout = Math.min(afterDeductible, remainingCap);\n      return {\n        payout: payout + nextPayout,\n        remainingCap: remainingCap - nextPayout,\n      };\n    },\n    { payout: 0, remainingCap: policyCap }\n  );\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const quoteItems = step.items ?? [];\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteItems, scenario.customer, results.length),\n      });\n      policies.push({ items: quoteItems, cap: policyCapFor(quoteItems) });\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy ?? 0];\n      const claimResult = calculateClaimResult(policy.cap, step, policy.items);\n      policy.cap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n      results.push(claimResult);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784924767917},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:198","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1 | head -30","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1680,"output":35,"cacheRead":116352,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3,"totalTokens":118067,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924767922,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-1c8b4f11-6a78-4535-a04c-55977bf5ff75","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:198","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (38 tests | 5 skipped) 6ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  33 passed | 5 todo (38)\n   Start at  20:26:10\n   Duration  166ms (transform 38ms, setup 0ms, collect 38ms, tests 6ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784924770706},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Continue. Test 34: unknown item type in quote.","thinkingSign