:"functions.bash:9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"node -e \"\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst src = fs.readFileSync('src/claim-office.ts','utf8');\n// strip comments\nlet code = src.replace(/\\/\\/.*$/gm,'').replace(/\\/\\*[\\s\\S]*?\\*\\//g,'');\n// strip type-only lines (interface, type) to avoid counting them\nconst runtime = code.replace(/^\\s*type\\s+\\w+\\s*=.*$/gm,'').replace(/^\\s*interface\\s+\\w+\\s*\\{[\\s\\S]*?\\n\\s*\\}/gm,'');\n// constants\nconst nums = (runtime.match(/\\b\\d+(\\.\\d+)?\\b/g) || []).length;\nconst strs = (runtime.match(/(['\\\"\\`])((?:\\\\\\1|.)*?)\\1/g) || []).length;\nconst bools = (runtime.match(/\\b(true|false|null|undefined)\\b/g) || []).length;\nconst constants = nums + strs + bools;\n// bindings: const/let/var identifiers (simple, not destructuring count)\nconst decls = (runtime.match(/\\b(const|let|var)\\b/g) || []).length;\n// rough param count: count identifiers in function/arrow parameter lists by counting words before ) that are typed\n// simpler: count ':' type annotations inside parameter lists? Hard.\n// We'll count every function parameter by regexing parameter patterns.\nconst paramMatches = runtime.match(/\\(([^)]*)\\)\\s*(?::\\s*\\w+)?\\s*=>|\\bfunction\\s+\\w*\\s*\\(([^)]*)\\)|\\b\\w+\\s*\\(([^)]*)\\)\\s*:\\s*\\w+/g) || [];\nlet params = 0;\nfor (const m of paramMatches) {\n  const inner = m.replace(/^\\(/,'').replace(/\\)\\s*=>.*$/,'').replace(/\\):.*$/,')').replace(/^.*\\(/,'').replace(/\\).*$/,'');\n  const ids = inner.split(',').map(s=>s.trim()).filter(s=>s && !s.match(/^[.]{3}$/));\n  params += ids.length;\n}\n// invocations\nconst invocations = (runtime.match(/\\b\\w+\\s*\\(/g) || []).length;\n// conditionals: if + ternary ?\nconst ifs = (runtime.match(/\\bif\\b/g) || []).length;\nconst ternaries = (runtime.match(/(?<!\\?)\\?(?!\\?|\\.|\\s*=>)/g) || []).length;\nconst conditionals = ifs + ternaries;\n// loops\nconst fors = (runtime.match(/\\bfor\\b/g) || []).length;\nconst higher = (runtime.match(/\\b(reduce|forEach|map|filter|some|find|every)\\s*\\(/g) || []).length;\nconst loops = fors + higher;\n// assignments: = not part of ==/===/!=/!==/<=/>=/=>\nconst assignments = (runtime.match(/(?<![=!<>])=(?![=])/g) || []).length;\nconsole.log({constants, decls, params, invocations, conditionals, loops, assignments});\nconst total = constants + decls + params + invocations*2 + conditionals*4 + loops*5 + assignments*6;\nconsole.log('Total approx mass:', total);\n\"\n","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1753,"output":1983,"cacheRead":26816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1168,"totalTokens":30552,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924879877,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-729365d4-72d7-4766-ab72-340802717642","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  constants: 50,\n  decls: 57,\n  params: 35,\n  invocations: 49,\n  conditionals: 11,\n  loops: 10,\n  assignments: 78\n}\nTotal approx mass: 802\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784924893320},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The script is very rough; total 802. This seems high due to overcounting assignments (maybe counted many = in type annotations/object literals) and params. Not super useful. We could refine but not necessary. The script counted assignments 78, constants 50, etc. The reorganization and function change don't affect most counts except assignments/conditionals/bindings. The function change: old function had 3 assignments, 3 bindings, 2 conditionals; new has 1 assignment, 1 binding, 2 conditionals. So delta: -2 assignments, -2 bindings. Mass delta = -2*6 -2*1 = -14, consistent with our manual. The script's global counts may show difference if we compute old. But not needed.\n\nWe can report function-level mass. We should also m